import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateReachableWireMonoid
import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateReversibleWire
import AxQM.Concrete.FourGateUniversality

/-!
# The reachable circuit matrices are operators of a register `Evolution` submonoid
(N&C Exercise 4.43, four-gate bridge — the combined matrix→`Evolution` connection)

The four-gate universality bridge (Exercise 4.43) must exhibit the *abstract* reachable circuit set
of `Concrete.exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_reachableCircuits` — the submonoid
`Concrete.reachableCircuits finFunctionFinEquiv θ` of `Matrix (Fin 2ⁿ⁺¹) (Fin 2ⁿ⁺¹) ℂ`, dense in
`U(2ⁿ⁺¹)` up to a global phase — as circuits of the grounded `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` gates. The
two generator families of the reachable gate set have each been re-expressed as register `Evolution`
gates: the reachable single-qubit rotations on a wire as members of the register wire submonoid
`reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ` (`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableWireMonoid.lean`,
`exists_reachableRotationWireEvolution_op_eq`), and the `≤ 2`-control reversible gates as the named
register gates `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht`
(`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReversibleWire.lean`). This file **combines** the two into a single
register `Evolution` submonoid and identifies the reachable circuit set with it, one operator at a
time — the register-level counterpart of the abstract matrix submonoid `reachableCircuits`.

## What is formalised

* `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ` — the **register-level reachable circuit submonoid**: the
  submonoid of `Evolution (qudit 2ⁿ⁺¹)` generated by the two register generator families — the whole
  per-wire reachable-rotation submonoids `reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ` (all wires `j`) and
  the `≤ 2`-control reversible gates `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht` (`|S| ≤ 2`, `t ∉ S`). Its
  members are exactly the `Evolution`s whose operators are the reachable circuit matrices — the
  register-gate counterpart of `Concrete.reachableCircuits finFunctionFinEquiv θ`.
* `exists_reachableCircuitEvolution_op_eq` — **the matrix→submonoid bridge (operator form)**: every
  matrix `M ∈ Concrete.reachableCircuits finFunctionFinEquiv θ` is the operator of some member `E`
  of `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`:

    `E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM M`.

  Proved by `Submonoid.closure_induction` over the reachable circuit set. On a generator (a member
  of `reachableGateSet`): a reachable single-qubit rotation on a wire `j`
  (`singleQubitOnWire finFunctionFinEquiv j g`, `g ∈ reachableRotations θ`) is the operator of a
  member of `reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ` (the per-wire bridge
  `exists_reachableRotationWireEvolution_op_eq`), which sits inside the combined generating set; a
  `≤ 2`-control reversible gate `permGate finFunctionFinEquiv (mcNotPerm S ht)`
  (`IsToffoliPermGate`) is, by definition, the operator of `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht`
  (`quditGate_op`), also a generator. The `1` / product cases are the multiplicativity of
  `Evolution.op`
  (`Evolution.id_op` / `Evolution.comp_op`) and of `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` (`map_one` / `map_mul`).
  The whole-circuit analogue of the single-family `exists_reachableRotationWireEvolution_op_eq`.

This is the register-side identification the density transport
(`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableCircuitDensity.lean`) promotes: the matrix density statement
`exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_reachableCircuits`, transported through the continuous `⋆`-algebra
isomorphism `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM`, lands in the closure of the operator image of
`reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`; the whole-submonoid register lift then re-expresses each such
`Evolution` as a grounded `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` circuit on the tower.

The bridge statement is in terms of the reachable circuit matrices (`Concrete.reachableCircuits`,
`Concrete.singleQubitOnWire`, `Concrete.permGate`) and `Evolution.op` / `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM`.
It is placed beside `AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableWireMonoid.lean` (whose per-wire
submonoid it collects) and `AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReversibleWire.lean` (whose
`mcNotWireEvolution` it collects).
-/

open Matrix

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

open AxQM.Concrete

/-- **The register-level reachable circuit submonoid.** The submonoid of `Evolution (qudit 2ⁿ⁺¹)`
generated by the two register generator families realising the reachable gate set: the whole
per-wire reachable-rotation submonoids `reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ` (over every wire
`j`), and the `≤ 2`-control reversible gates `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht` (`|S| ≤ 2`, `t ∉ S`)
— the `Toffoli`/`CNOT`/`NOT` register gates. The register-gate counterpart of the abstract matrix
submonoid `Concrete.reachableCircuits finFunctionFinEquiv θ`; its members are exactly the
`Evolution`s whose operators are reachable circuit matrices
(`exists_reachableCircuitEvolution_op_eq`). -/
noncomputable def reachableCircuitEvolutions (n : ℕ) (θ : ℝ) :
    Submonoid (Evolution (qudit (2 ^ (n + 1)))) :=
  Submonoid.closure
    ((⋃ j : Fin (n + 1),
        (reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ : Set (Evolution (qudit (2 ^ (n + 1)))))) ∪
      {E | ∃ (S : Finset (Fin (n + 1))) (t : Fin (n + 1)) (ht : t ∉ S),
        S.card ≤ 2 ∧ E = mcNotWireEvolution (n + 1) S t ht})

/-- **The reachable circuit matrices are operators of the register circuit submonoid.** Every matrix
`M ∈ Concrete.reachableCircuits finFunctionFinEquiv θ` is the operator of some member `E` of the
register submonoid `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`:

  `E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM M`.

Proved by `Submonoid.closure_induction` over the reachable circuit set `reachableGateSet`. On a
generator: a reachable single-qubit rotation on a wire `j` (`singleQubitOnWire finFunctionFinEquiv j
g`, `g ∈ reachableRotations θ`) is, by the per-wire bridge
`exists_reachableRotationWireEvolution_op_eq`, the operator of a member of
`reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ` — a generator of the combined submonoid; a `≤ 2`-control
reversible gate `permGate finFunctionFinEquiv (mcNotPerm S ht)` (`IsToffoliPermGate`) is, by
definition (`quditGate_op`), the operator of `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht`, also a generator.
The unit maps to `1`; products are carried by the multiplicativity of both `Evolution.op`
(`Evolution.comp_op`) and `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` (`map_mul`). The whole-circuit analogue of the
single-family `exists_reachableRotationWireEvolution_op_eq`; the register-side identification the
density transport promotes onto the grounded `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` gate set. -/
theorem exists_reachableCircuitEvolution_op_eq {n : ℕ} {θ : ℝ}
    {M : Matrix (Fin (2 ^ (n + 1))) (Fin (2 ^ (n + 1))) ℂ}
    (hM : M ∈ Concrete.reachableCircuits finFunctionFinEquiv θ) :
    ∃ E ∈ reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ,
      E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin (2 ^ (n + 1))) M := by
  induction hM using Submonoid.closure_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    rcases hx with hperm | hrot
    · -- `≤ 2`-control reversible gate: the operator of `mcNotWireEvolution`.
      obtain ⟨S, t, ht, hcard, rfl⟩ := hperm
      exact ⟨mcNotWireEvolution (n + 1) S t ht,
        Submonoid.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨S, t, ht, hcard, rfl⟩), quditGate_op _⟩
    · -- reachable single-qubit rotation on a wire `j`: a member of the per-wire submonoid.
      simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, Set.mem_image] at hrot
      obtain ⟨j, g, hg, rfl⟩ := hrot
      obtain ⟨F, hF, hFop⟩ := exists_reachableRotationWireEvolution_op_eq (n := n) (t := j) hg
      exact ⟨F, Submonoid.subset_closure (Or.inl (Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨j, hF⟩)), hFop⟩
  | one =>
    refine ⟨1, one_mem _, ?_⟩
    rw [Evolution.one_def, Evolution.id_op]
    exact (map_one Matrix.toEuclideanCLM).symm
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    obtain ⟨Ex, hEx, hExop⟩ := ihx
    obtain ⟨Ey, hEy, hEyop⟩ := ihy
    refine ⟨Ex * Ey, mul_mem hEx hEy, ?_⟩
    rw [Evolution.mul_def, Evolution.comp_op, hExop, hEyop]
    exact (map_mul Matrix.toEuclideanCLM x y).symm

end

end AxQM
